<title>USA: High Plains Wheat-Farmer sales slow, demand light.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat-Farmer sales slow, demand light.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mostly steady on Tuesday, underpinned by slow farmer sales, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Sluggish export demand, however, led to weakness at some locations. There was also some concern that this week's CCC catalog sale may increase availability and spark some weakness during the next few days.</p>
<p>Many farmers in Kansas remained preoccupied with harvesting other crops. The weekly state crop report, issued Monday, put the Kansas sorghum harvest at 77 percent complete as of Sunday, corn at 93 percent and soybeans at 82 percent.  </p>
